{
 "info": {
  "name": "Imcorpcart Partner API",
  "description": "Machine-to-machine Partner API for Imcorpcart (`/partner-api/v1`).\n\n## Setup\n1. Import this collection **and** one of the environment files (Dev or Prod).\n2. Pick an environment from the top-right dropdown (**Imcorpcart Partner \u2013 Dev** or **\u2026 Prod**).\n3. Open the environment, paste your bearer token into the `token` variable, and Save.\n4. Run any request \u2014 auth (`Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`) is inherited by every request.\n\n## Notes\n- **All list parameters are query-string parameters, not a request body.** A JSON body on a GET request is ignored.\n- `category` is a category **slug** (lowercase, e.g. `phones`), not a display name.\n- Prices returned are *your* price: set by imcorpcart for each product, commission included, alongside the `mrp` list price. The catalogue is a snapshot \u2014 price and availability are re-validated at order time with structured error codes.\n- `externalRef` on an order is your own order id and the dedup key: re-posting the same value returns the existing order (`200`, `duplicate:true`) instead of creating a second one.\n\n## Following an order\n\nYou pull; there is nothing to host and nothing to subscribe to. Call **List orders** with `updatedSince` set to the previous response's `meta.syncedAt`, and keep the new `syncedAt` for the next call. The window overlaps on purpose \u2014 reads are idempotent, so a repeat is harmless and nothing is missed. Omit `updatedSince` for a first full sync.\n\n`updatedSince` catches every change that matters, including ones that never touch the order record: a courier scan and a proof of delivery being attached both bring the order back on your next poll.\n\nEvery order carries `statusCode` (stable \u2014 switch on this: CONFIRMED \u00b7 DISPATCHED \u00b7 IN_TRANSIT \u00b7 OUT_FOR_DELIVERY \u00b7 DELIVERED \u00b7 CANCELLED \u00b7 RETURNED \u00b7 FAILED) and `status` (the label \u2014 display this). Status follows the **shipment**, so In Transit and Out for Delivery are distinct.\n\nRate limit: **120 requests per minute per token** (`RateLimit-*` headers on every response).",
  "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
 },
 "auth": {
  "type": "bearer",
  "bearer": [
   {
    "key": "token",
    "value": "{{token}}",
    "type": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "variable": [
  {
   "key": "baseUrl",
   "value": "https://imcorp.heptanesia.com/api/partner-api/v1",
   "type": "string"
  }
 ],
